# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Cloned corpus repos. Reproducible from the slugs in the manifests, and far too
# large to version (543MB for five repos).
.cache/

# Mined label sets from v2 onward. These are *derived* data: the deterministic
# output of (repo shas, commit window, MineConfig, code version), and one day of
# iteration produced seven of them totalling 16MB. What gets versioned instead is
# the provenance -- `data/*.manifest.json` records every input plus a sha256 of
# the output, and its `replay` field regenerates the file byte-identically. That
# was verified, not assumed, before this rule was added.
#
# `data/labels.jsonl` (v1) is deliberately NOT ignored. It predates manifests, so
# it is the one label set that cannot be regenerated, and the hand-labelled
# verdicts in review/ join to it by `example_id`. Losing it would make the
# ground-truth sheets unattributable.
data/labels-v*.jsonl

# The stage-2c reading bundle: 98 files, 1.2MB, copied verbatim out of five
# upstream projects so a reviewer can read them (the clones are bare, so there is
# no working tree to open). Ignored because it is neither ours nor irreplaceable
# -- `driftwood doc-sample` regenerates it byte-identically from the trees the
# sheet itself pins, and vendoring other projects' source into this repo would
# add their licences to ours for no gain. `review/2c/SHEET.md` is NOT ignored:
# that one is the ground truth.
review/2c/text/

# Credentials. Stage 3's model arm reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the environment and
# nothing here ever writes it down, so these patterns guard against a habit rather
# than against this code: a `.env` dropped in to try something, an editor's backup of
# one. This repository is public, and a pushed key is a key that has to be revoked
# rather than deleted -- `git rm` does not unpublish it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*

# Agent configuration. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` is the project instructions for this repo, and it
# is deliberately local: it exists partly to state what must NOT be published from here, which
# is not itself a thing to publish. Ignored rather than left untracked because an untracked file
# in a public repository is one careless `git add` from being outward-facing.
#
# That is the whole reason. This path is NOT a containment control: AGENTS.md is not preloaded as
# project instructions on Claude Code 2.1.278, so a CLAUDE.md here suppresses nothing.
.claude/

# IDE state. PyCharm rewrites `.idea/` constantly and some of what it puts there is
# machine-specific rather than project-specific -- local interpreter paths, run
# configurations, scratch state. Ignored for the same reason as the line above: an
# untracked directory in a public repository is one careless `git add` from being
# outward-facing, and this one reappears on its own every time the project is opened.
.idea/

# Never ignored, and worth saying why:
#   review/*.md              -- the hand labels. Irreplaceable; every number
#                               downstream is measured against them.
#   review/2c/SHEET.md       -- same, for the hand-labelled retrieval corpus.
#   data/scores/*.json       -- the measurement history. A result is data, not
#                               console output.
#   data/*.manifest.json     -- what makes the ignored files above regenerable.
